What does Video Editor do at WPP Production?
&nbsp;
As a Video Editor, you will be attending to day-to-day adaptation work with a primary master to deliver across the international markets. This will require strong Premiere Pro and After Effects skills and an excellent understanding of international broadcast standards.&nbsp;

Responsibilities:

• Editing, Re-Editing according to the story boards and/or briefs to arrive at the required duration of the commercial while keeping the essential story/message intact.&nbsp;

• Incorporate various artworks, graphics and renders got from various other departments strictly following the given file management structure.&nbsp;

• Building Broadcast clocks according to delivery specs&nbsp;

• Laying sound mix and measuring the audio meter to ensure it fits the delivery standard&nbsp;

• Adding legal lines in their right templates and duration for various markets.&nbsp;

• Changing product packs and motion graphic elements in After Effects

• Ensuring all broadcast material is 100% compliant for target market in legal and technical standards.

Requirements:

• Strong Adobe Premiere and After Effects&nbsp;

• Strong Editing and Motion Graphics skills.&nbsp;

• Strong understanding of Standards, Frame Rates, Aspect Ratios and Audio Specs.&nbsp;

• Proven experience working on commercials for large brands delivering to international markets.&nbsp;

• A good understanding of current Asian, American, UK and European broadcast requirements.&nbsp;

• Great attention to detail to identify quality, size and colour mismatches on the go.&nbsp;

• Ability to work in a fast-paced environment which demands varied set of rules to be followed across multiple clients and markets.&nbsp;

